       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '154152778X', 'average_rating': 2.8}, page_content=\"Earth-Friendly Animal Crafts (Green STEAM) Paperback – August 1, 2018 None Veronica Thompson (Author, Photographer) Books Children's Books Science, Nature & How It Works About the Author Veronica Thompson lives in a little brownstone in Brooklyn, New York, with her two puppies and wonderful husband. She spends her days crafting for her website, makescoutdiy.com, and building websites. Animal lovers will adore these hands-on projects, which use recycled materials to make animal-themed crafts. Photos and detailed instructions walk readers through each step. Convert a recycled jar into a retro bird feeder, turn recycled paper into wild lion wall art, and transform old T-shirts into a dog toy. A QR code provides a link to additional how-to photos for each activity.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1947645102', 'average_rating': 3.9}, page_content='Good Habits Part 1 (Booklet): A 3-in-1 unique book teaching children Good Habits, Values as well as types of Animals (Positive Learning for Kids) Paperback – November 2, 2017 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71KmZY4pEEL._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Ankit Kothari\\', \\'about\\': [\"Ankit Kothari is an inventor, author and a motivator, but the most important of all, he is a proud father of two young kids. \\'Positive Learning for Kids\\' series is truly a passion project for Ankit Kothari with an honest intent to teach positive concepts, good habits and values to children all around the world. Other than books, Ankit also loves to invent new things, which is apparent from his numerous patents in the fields of self-driving cars, smartphones, augmented reality, etc. Ankit has also been recognized by many news channels and newspapers around the United States as well as internationally for his various achievements in a number of fields.\"]} Ankit Kothari (Author) Books Children\\'s Books Growing Up & Facts of Life  Positive Learning for Kids: Good Habits Part 1 is a 3-in-1 unique book which teaches good habits, values as well as types of animals to children. This book features photos of real animals creatively demonstrating good habits as well as core values to children and enabling parents to teach such positive life skills to children at an early age.Parenting can sometimes be difficult when you have to constantly remind your children to \"Do this...\", \"Do this...\", \"Don\\'t do that...\", \"Don\\'t do that...\", etc. Wouldn\\'t it be great if you can teach good habits to your children in a creative way such that they always remember those good habits and in fact practice them on a daily basis. Well, that\\'s exactly why we created this book - \\'Good Habits Part 1\\' to solve that problem!By teaching good habits in a fun and easy way with the help of real animals, this book intends to help the parents integrate those vital concepts into their children\\'s daily routine without any difficulties. \\'Good Habits Part 1\\' fits in perfectly within the \\'Positive Learning for Kids\\' series, which not only makes learning fun for kids but also makes life easy for a busy parent. \\'Positive Learning for Kids\\' is truly an innovative series that aims to bring a positive change in children\\'s day-to-day learning and build a solid foundation that helps them attain unstoppable success and prosperity in future - \"Learn Positively and Live with Positivity!\" PS: Please also check out the following books in \\'Positive Learning for Kids\\' series, which are equally as amazing as this \\'Good Habits Part 1\\' book - (1) Good Habits Part 2 (2) Animal Alphabet A to Z (3) Animal Alphabet Sharing and Caring'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1502319403', 'average_rating': 4.6}, page_content='Melancholy (Jokers\\' Wrath MC) Paperback – September 9, 2014 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amzn-author-media-prod/tluiisep88llakc08ngr7l2e99._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Bella Jewel\\', \\'about\\': [\"Bella Jewel, also known as Bec Botefuhr, has been writing since she was just shy of fifteen years old. With multiple USA Today Bestselling titles, traditionally published books, foreign published books, and audio deals, she keeps herself busy and has no plans on stopping soon. Living in sunny Queensland, Australia, you can find Bella spending time with her family when she\\'s not busy tapping at the keys. She enjoys the outdoors, camping, fishing, and boating, but mostly, she enjoys books! Reading and writing are her passion!\", \\'You can find and follow her using the link below.\\', \\'https://linktr.ee/bellajewel\\']} Bella Jewel (Author) Books Romance Contemporary  \"There\\'s never been a time I\\'ve cared about anything more than my club. Today that all changed. Today I got you.\" Maddox is the President of the Jokers\\' Wrath MC. He\\'s hard, he\\'s determined and he\\'s never had to give his heart over…until the day he found and saved Santana. Sassy and head-strong, she\\'s given him a run for his money for a solid five years. Their tension has built and both of them have danced around a passion that\\'s burning so deep in their souls, it\\'s all-consuming. They want each other - they\\'re just too stubborn to admit it. Heat, lust and sassy natures will have them fighting against what\\'s real. She\\'s feisty, he\\'s stubborn. But everything will change the moment she gets her first taste of the rugged, broody biker. There\\'s one problem with this story...Maddox has a secret. A secret he knows will crush Santana. It will take her life and spiral it out of control, sending them into a world of danger that will risk not only their lives, but everyone in the clubs, too. Will their love withstand the battle? Or will Maddox lose the only girl he\\'s loved, forever?'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1535097620', 'average_rating': 4.0}, page_content='Hidden Blade (The Soul Eater) Paperback – July 6, 2016 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amzn-author-media-prod/utrpo1j9984frh45cutuk37js0._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Pippa DaCosta\\', \\'about\\': [\\'Born in Kent, UK, Pippa\\\\\\'s published books have featured in--- \"Wait a second. Let\\\\\\'s cut to the chase. I write kick-a$$ urban fantasy novels with conflicted characters, breathless action, and no-holds-barred dialogue. My books may not leave you feeling all fluffy and warm inside, but they will excite you. There will be plot-wists, there will be angst, probably a few dead bodies, and very likely your favorite character will turn out to be the bad guy. Don\\\\\\'t say I didn\\\\\\'t want you...\"\\', \"Pippa\\'s family moved to the South West of England where she grew up amongst the dramatic moorland and sweeping coastlands of Devon & Cornwall. With a family history brimming with intrigue, complete with Romani angst on one side and Jewish survivors on another, she has the ability to draw from a patchwork of ancestry and use it as the inspiration for her writing. Happily married and the Mother of two little girls, she resides on the Devon & Cornwall border.\", \"Visit www.pippadacosta.com to see what she\\'s working on today.\"]} Pippa DaCosta (Author) Books Literature & Fiction Genre Fiction Review \"Brilliant world building, fascinating mythology, wonderful multilayered characters that you will either love or love to hate and a fast moving storyline that will keep you turning the pages until the end.\" Feeling Fictional \"There is just something about Pippa\\'s writing whether it\\'s her smartass enticing characters or her gut-squeezing action scenes that keep you on the edge of your seats.\" Kariny\\'s Boox Frenzy \"Multilayered characters, great actions scenes and an emotional rollercoaster.\" Accidental Reader \"They call me devil, liar, thief. In whispers, they call me Soul Eater. They’re right. I’m all those things—and more.\" Kicked out of the underworld and cursed to walk this earth for all eternity, Ace Dante finds solace in helping others avoid the wrath of the gods.But when warrior-bitch, Queen of Cats, and Ace\\'s ex-wife, Bastet, hires him to stop whoever is slaughtering her blessed women, Ace is caught between two of the most powerful deities to have ever existed: Isis and Osiris.The once-revered gods aren’t dead.They’re back.And Ace is in their way.Welcome to a New York where the ancient gods roam.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0575073357', 'average_rating': 3.7}, page_content=\"The Man in the High Castle (S.F.Masterworks) U.K. Hardcover – January 1, 2001 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71Ml-t-wqNL._SY600_.jpg', 'name': 'Philip K. Dick', 'about': ['Over a writing career that spanned three decades, Philip K. Dick (1928-1982) published 36 science fiction novels and 121 short stories in which he explored the essence of what makes man human and the dangers of centralized power. Toward the end of his life, his work turned toward deeply personal, metaphysical questions concerning the nature of God. Eleven novels and short stories have been adapted to film; notably: Blade Runner (based on Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?), Total Recall, Minority Report, and A Scanner Darkly. The recipient of critical acclaim and numerous awards throughout his career, Dick was inducted into the Science Fiction Hall of Fame in 2005, and in 2007 the Library of America published a selection of his novels in three volumes. His work has been translated into more than twenty-five languages.']} Philip K. Dick (Author) Books Science Fiction & Fantasy Science Fiction  The Man in the High Castle (SF Masterworks)\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0978636503', 'average_rating': 5.0}, page_content='Understanding the Latin Mass: Hear and Learn the Words of the Novus Ordo Spiral-bound – January 1, 2006 None Marion P. Smedberg (Author)   An account of the Novus Ordo, the latin mass. A word-by-word latin text of the mass with english translation. An accompaying Audio CD provides the spoken words. Includes a basic introduction to latin.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0595214088', 'average_rating': 4.8}, page_content='The Death Valley Kids Paperback – March 1, 2002 None Giovanni Capurro (Author) Books Literature & Fiction Genre Fiction About the Author Giovanni Capurro was born somewhere in greater Los Angeles, which is where he currently resides. He has also lived in and around Panama, Argentina, San Francisco, Atlanta and Washington, DC. He says he is working on a second novel, but really, who can ever tell? Four friends come of age on the lam from Johnny Law in this lacerating satire on Post-Modern Americana.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '3639306120', 'average_rating': 5.0}, page_content='Transformational Leadership: A Case Study of a Failed Multinational-Owned Company Becoming a Successful Locally-Owned Enterprise Paperback – November 19, 2010 None Syed Haider (Author) Books Business & Money Management & Leadership  A case study of market conditions and organizational factors including, leadership style, culture, mission and strategy was conducted to examine and analyze the economic performance and profitability of a subsidiary of a multinational firm operating in Pakistan under two circumstances: first, as a subsidiary of a multinational corporation and later, as a locally-owned Pakistani business. An analysis of a ten-year history of performance and market conditions revealed market conditions alone did not explain the steady and profitable performance of the locally-owned company as compared to its performance under multinational ownership. Instead, strategic and entrepreneurial leadership, a flat organizational structure, emphasis on customer service, product quality, state-of-the art plant technology, teamwork, employee motivation and empowerment, open communication, and a mindset for continuous improvement were the critical factors associated with the turnaround of a former multinational firm from a failed enterprise to a successful business venture.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B08H6ZLMHM', 'average_rating': 4.2}, page_content=\"Gaston Hall (Tales from The Parlor Room: A Collection of Gothic and Ghostly Tales) Kindle Edition None L.B. Stimson (Author),  Gabriella Messina (Editor)   Format: Kindle Edition Books Literature & Fiction Genre Fiction  Set against the backdrop of the U.S. Civil War, the residents of Gaston Hall find themselves struggling to survive in a place where the worlds of both the living and the dead are intertwined. All is not what it may seem at Gaston Hall—a home for orphaned and abandoned children. One. Two. Three. Four. The children appeared. “Ashes. Ashes. We all tumbled down.” Della’s eyes fluttered. She shifted in her chair; her mouth pinched. Elsie drew back as the smallest and last of the spectres emerged. The child crawled upon Della’s lap, nestling her head against her mother’s breast. Della’s chin dropped, disappearing within her daughter’s matted hair. The others began to sway, moving around their mother and sister in a close circle and humming the horrific tune. Elsie watched in horror but remained firm in her place. Were the children sending her clues or taunting their mother? It couldn't be. Oh, what wicked thing did you do? Elsie leaned close to the woman’s face and whispered in her ear. “What did you do to your children?”\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1571688927', 'average_rating': 4.7}, page_content='Blood of Noble Men Paperback – January 5, 2006 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61vWgpWJeIL._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Alan C. Huffines\\', \\'about\\': [\\'Alan C. Huffines is a retired military officer and combat veteran of two conflicts. He is the author of \"Blood of Noble Men: The Alamo Siege and Battle, an Illustrated Chronology\", \"A Pilgrim Shadow\", \"The Texas War of Independence\", and \"Killed by Indians 1871.\" He serves as military editor for True West and as a columnist for Working Ranch magazines. He has provided historical work on numerous feature films and documentaries. He was a featured author at the 1999 and 2001 Texas Book Festival and has appeared on CSPAN’s \"Book TV.\"\\', \\'He is an eighth generation Texan and married to the former Caroline Cotham of North Carolina; they have four children and make their home in Buffalo Gap, Texas.\\']} Alan C. Huffines (Author),  Gary S. Zaboly (Illustrator) Books History Americas Review At last an Alamo book that gives us a day-by-day account utilizing the wide spectrum of participant accounts. Native Texan Alan Huffines has given us the Alamo book for the end of the century with magnificent illustrations by renowned historical artist Gary Zaboly. Huffines manages to present the Alamo story in a straightforward manner without becoming bogged down in historical and emotional diatribes that have so plagued recent Alamo works. Alamo students will definitely want this one for easy reference while it is the one book Alamo visitors should have with them while visiting the site. Every Alamo book has its faults, but this is a work that has been needed for years. --The Journal of the Alamo Battlefield Association About the Author Alan C. Huffines is an eighth-generation Texan, Persian Gulf War veteran, and retired active duty combat arms officer. He holds both a B.A. and an M.A. in history and has been published in Military Collector and Historian and The Journal of the Alamo Battlefield Association. Huffines is a member of the Company of Military Historians, Texas State Historical Association, the Alamo Society, National Guard Association of Texas, National Infantry Association (Lone Star Chapter) and is a charter board member of the Alamo Battlefield Association. He and his wife, the former Caroline Cotham, have four children\\xa0and make their home in Buffalo Gap,\\xa0Texas. This was\\xa0his first book. The Alamo and its defenders, according to historian Stephen L. Hardin, \"transcended mere history; both entered the realm of myth.\" Indeed, the siege and battle of the Alamo serves today as a definition of American character. The date of March 6, 1836, is forever ensconced in the annals of history. But what happened in the twelve days leading up to the final battle of March 6? And did events transpire in the final battle as history has led us to believe? As Hardin stated in the foreword for this book, \"Myth has so shrouded every aspect of the Alamo story that it becomes hard to separate the factual from the fanciful. Understand and appreciate the myth. Understand and appreciate the historical reality. But, please, graze them in different pastures.\" Author Alan Huffines has researched both the history and the myth of the Alamo. What he found lacking in Alamo accounts was a perspective unaffected by either history or myth. In this book he portrays the events preliminary to and during the battle from the viewpoint of the participants. In a day-by-day chronology of the thirteen days, he presents original Texian and Mexican perspectives so that the reader may decide which may be accurate and which possibly embellished. His critical analysis of the participants\\' reports, through extensive annotation, points out inconsistencies and provides considerable food for thought. The renowned military artist Gary S. Zaboly fastidiously researched primary sources for accuracy in clothing, weapons, architecture, geography, and so on, resulting in maps and artwork that offer a new visual perspective of the Alamo and those who were involved with the siege. Through the author\\'s research and the artist\\'s fine illustrations, the thirteen days come into focus, and the people who experienced the sights, smells, sounds, and emotions of that two-week period are allowed \"to speak finally for themselves.\"'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B000UUMOB8', 'average_rating': 5.0}, page_content='Spider-Man Maximum Clonage Alpha #1 : And the Jackal Cries Death (Marvel Comics) Comic – August 1, 1995 None Todd DeFalco, Tom; DeZago (Author) Books Comics & Graphic Novels Publishers  Direct Edition w/ barcode. (barcode is on back cover). Wraparound acetate cover!! Looks Unbelievable!!'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '061813171X', 'average_rating': 3.5}, page_content=\"The Last Voyage of Somebody the Sailor Paperback – November 20, 2001 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'John Barth', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} John Barth (Author) Books Literature & Fiction United States About the Author JOHN BARTH\\x92s fiction has won the National Book Award, the PEN/Malamud Award, and the Lannan Foundation Lifetime Achievement Award. For many years he taught in the Writing Seminars at John Hopkins University. He is the author of such seminal works as The Sot-Weed Factor, Chimera (for which he won the NBA), and Giles Goat-Boy. \\x93Toga Party,\\x94 an excerpt from The Development, appeared in The Best American Short Stories 2007, edited by Stephen King. While retracing the legendary voyages of Sindbad the Sailor, journalist Simon William Behler finds himself in Sindbad's household in medieval Baghdad and competes with Sindbad in a storytelling marathon in the hopes of finding way back to the modern world. Reprint.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B08TQ4F35M', 'average_rating': 3.6}, page_content=\"Quantum Physics for Beginners: Understanding the Universe and How Our Reality Works by Simplified Explanation of the Principles of Quantum Physics Paperback – January 21, 2021 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'Brandon Steel', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} Brandon Steel (Author) Books Science & Math Biological Sciences  If you want to peek into the fascinating Quantum world but don’t know where to begin, keep reading as this book lays out the science behind quantum physics in a clear and accessible language! Are you fascinated by the Universe? Do you believe in its power? Would you like to gain a better understanding of how everything works? There’s much more to quantum physics than you might think; once you realize how it affects our everyday life, you’d wish you started learning sooner! Would you like to: Learn about the history of quantum physics and why it is so important? Learn about the history of quantum physics and why it is so important? Make learning quantum physics fun and rewarding experience? Make learning quantum physics fun and rewarding experience? Be able to clearly see how quantum physics governs our lives? Be able to clearly see how quantum physics governs our lives? Peel away the layers of mystery concerning our Universe? Peel away the layers of mystery concerning our Universe? The journey to understanding quantum physics is the journey of shattering your limited views of our world. And, this book will be your tour guide; you’ll see how enthralling our reality is and how your thoughts translate into the Universe. This realization will make you aware of your own power in changing your reality through the law of attraction! These are a few of the topics that this book discusses: What is quantum physics, the history and basic concepts of quantum physics; What is quantum physics, the history and basic concepts of quantum physics; The law and principles of quantum physics and law of attraction; The law and principles of quantum physics and law of attraction; Were quantum physics is applied; Were quantum physics is applied; Exploration of the revolutionary works of Richard Feynman; Exploration of the revolutionary works of Richard Feynman; The invisible relation between waves and particles; The invisible relation between waves and particles; The Heisenberg uncertainty principle and Einstein’s theory of relativity; The Heisenberg uncertainty principle and Einstein’s theory of relativity; Franck-hertz experiments in the domain of quantum physics; Franck-hertz experiments in the domain of quantum physics; Wave interference and quantum entanglement; Wave interference and quantum entanglement; Instability of classical atoms; Instability of classical atoms; And much more! And much more! Even if this is the first time you’re hearing these terms, don’t be scared by the big words. The purpose of this book is to simplify quantum physics for beginners and make the subject interesting for the common man. And, this book fulfills its purpose! Scroll up, click on “Buy Now with 1-click”, and Get Your Copy Now!\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0836805267', 'average_rating': 4.7}, page_content=\"Dandelion's Vanishing Vegetable Garden (Beechwood Bunny Tales) Library Binding – January 1, 1991 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'Geneviève Huriet', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} Genevieve Huriet (Author),  Loic Jouannigot (Illustrator) Books Children's Books  While the other Bellflower bunny children plant vegetables in their garden, Dandelion decides to plant strawberries which soon become the target of a hungry turtle\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B004QOA9CU', 'average_rating': 1.7}, page_content=\"Journal of a Landscape Painter in Corsica Paperback – December 31, 2010 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'Edward Lear', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} Edward Lear (Author) Books Literature & Fiction Classics  Journal of a Landscape Painter in Corsica is presented here in a high quality paperback edition. This publication is a professional scan from an original edition of the book, and of the best possible quality. This popular classic work by Edward Lear is in the English language. If you enjoy the works of Edward Lear then we highly recommend this publication for your reading enjoyment.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B000ETQPYW', 'average_rating': 4.6}, page_content=\"Rotisserie Chickens to the Rescue! : How To Use the Already-Roasted Chickens You Purchase at the Market to Make More Than 125 Simple and Delicious Meals Paperback – Bargain Price, September 10, 2003 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'Carla Fitzgerald Williams', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} Carla Fitzgerald Williams (Author) Books Cookbooks, Food & Wine Quick & Easy  \"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1939346746', 'average_rating': 4.6}, page_content=\"Eternal Warrior: Days of Steel Paperback – Illustrated, July 14, 2015 {'avatar': 'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/01Kv-W2ysOL._SY600_.png', 'name': 'Peter Milligan', 'about': ['Discover more of the author’s books, see similar authors, read author blogs and more']} Peter Milligan (Author),  Cary Nord (Artist) Books Comics & Graphic Novels Graphic Novels  From steel comes salvation! The Eternal Warrior...Gilad Anni-Padda, the Earth’s Fist and Steel...is forever charged with guarding the Geomancer and securing the Earth’s safety. After completing another brutal mission, the Earth’s undying guardian is approached with a cryptic task: find and save a baby ― in whose hands might rest the fate of an entire people! But the Eternal Warrior is no nursemaid...and, to complicate matters, a thousand Magyar invaders want the baby dead. At the edge of civilization, can history’s most expert killer keep one precious life alive? From steel comes salvation! The Eternal Warrior...Gilad Anni-Padda, the Earth’s Fist and Steel...is forever charged with guarding the Geomancer and securing the Earth’s safety. After completing another brutal mission, the Earth’s undying guardian is approached with a cryptic task: find and save a baby ― in whose hands might rest the fate of an entire people! But the Eternal Warrior is no nursemaid...and, to complicate matters, a thousand Magyar invaders want the baby dead. At the edge of civilization, can history’s most expert killer keep one precious life alive? Start reading here as master storyteller Peter Milligan (Hellblazer) and Eisner Award-winning artist Cary Nord (X-O Manowar, Conan) chronicle the brutal and bloodied history of Valiant’s immortal champion in an all-new tale of swords, savagery, and steel. Start reading here as master storyteller Peter Milligan ( Hellblazer ) and Eisner Award-winning artist Cary Nord ( X-O Manowar , Conan ) chronicle the brutal and bloodied history of Valiant’s immortal champion in an all-new tale of swords, savagery, and steel. Collecting Eternal Warrior: Days of Steel #1–3. Collecting Eternal Warrior: Days of Steel #1–3.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B092P6ZMJX', 'average_rating': 4.7}, page_content='Maverick (Grim Sinners MC Originals) Paperback – April 17, 2021 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amzn-author-media-prod/h27hon89ml465f912fkdap9kkd._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'LeAnn Ashers\\', \\'about\\': [\\'USA Today Bestselling Author LeAnn Ashers is a blogger-turned-author who spends her days reading and writing.\\', \"She released her debut novel early 2016, and can\\'t wait to see where this adventure continues to take her.\", \\'LeAnn enjoys writing about strong-minded females and swoon-worthy, protective alpha males who love their women unconditionally.\\']} LeAnn Ashers (Author),  Wander Aquiar (Photographer) Books Literature & Fiction  BELLI grew up in a cult, one that kept me completely sheltered from the real life. They even forced me to marry at the age of fourteen.I was trapped, and life was utter hell until I was offered a way out. I spent months healing and finally being happy for the first time ever.Then he came into my life.Maverick rooted himself deep inside my heart from the second I met him. From his cocky grin to his alpha male attitude, I was in love with him.More importantly, he kept me safe when I needed him most.MAVERICKThe second I laid eyes on her, I knew she was the one I had waited for my whole life. All I saw was her.But everything came to a head when her past resurfaced.The second I saw the fear in her eyes, something inside me snapped. It became my life’s mission to find every single person who hurt her.After all, I am a Grim Sinner for a reason.It’s time to Reap.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0765305593', 'average_rating': 4.1}, page_content='The High City Hardcover – February 3, 2009 None Cecelia Holland (Author) Books Literature & Fiction Genre Fiction Review \"[Holland has] the hard, sharp lines of a master storyteller. She seems remarkably skillful at portraying the masculine mind.\" --Houston Chronicle \"We have come to expect rich, vivid historical novels from prolific Cecelia Holland, and this one, set in ninth century Constantinople, more than fulfills that expectation. We observe the legendary Byzantine duplicity through the eyes of our honorable barbarian hero as he tries to unravel the intrigue. Swiftly moving, plausible, and with just the right amount of historical details to make scenes come clear, the novel is an engrossing tale.\" -- Publishers Weekly on The Belt of Gold About the Author Cecelia Holland is widely acknowledged as one of the finest historical novelists of our time. She is the author of more than thirty novels, including The Angel and the Sword, Jerusalem, Lily Nevada, and The Kings in Winter. Holland lives in Humboldt County, in northern California, where she teaches creative writing, and is current at work on a new historical novel. It is the early years of the reign of Basil II, who became one most successful, and most feared, Byzantine emperors. But for now, Basil rules as a co-emperor with his brother Constantine, and makes war on a would-be usurper, Bardas Phokas, son of a General who Basil supplanted. Basil’s most trusted troops are foreign mercenaries, the Varangian guard hired from the North. Rus and Norsemen, Viking raiders and wild horsemen from the steppes, they fall upon the elegant city of Constantinople like wolves on a garden party. Among them is the wily young son of an Irish slave, who comes to the notice of the emperor’s wife. But being noticed by an angry emperor is not safe at all.'),\n",
