       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0825633761', 'average_rating': 4.7}, page_content='Encyclopedia Of Keyboard Color Picture Chords Plastic Comb – January 31, 2006 None Felipe Orozco (Author) Books Arts & Photography Music  Over 1000 essential keyboard chord positions in easy-to-read, color chord diagrams. This book includes: full-color photographs of each position, special two-handed chord voicings, chord theory section and chord progressions.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1075010799', 'average_rating': 5.0}, page_content='If You Need Me, I\\'ll Be At The River Hunting Arrowheads Journal: Lined Journal Diary Notebook 120 Pages, 6\" x 9\" (15.24 x 22.86 cm), Durable Soft Cover Paperback – June 19, 2019 None TCAN Family Press (Author) Books Education & Teaching Studying & Workbooks  We hope you’ll enjoy our Journal Notebooks in the 6 x 9 inch; 15.24 x 22.86 cm size as much as we did creating it for you. Write and journal your arrowhead adventures. Journal features include: 120 lined white pages, gorgeous designed cover, Size 6 x 9 inch; 15.24 x 22.86 cm dimensions; the ideal size for all purposes, fitting perfectly into your bag, briefcase, back pack or satchel. The bold white paper is sturdy enough to be used with fountain pens, Reliable standards: Book industry perfect binding (the same standard binding as the books in your local library), Tough matte paperback. Crisp white paper, with quality that minimizes ink bleed-through, The book is great for either pen or pencil users. Journals are the perfect gift for finding your treasures.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0976056402', 'average_rating': 4.5}, page_content='Galahad 1: The Comet\\'s Curse Paperback – November 10, 2004 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amzn-author-media-prod/2fei5lpjv7k3ibi6hbttfpq26u._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Dom Testa\\', \\'about\\': [\\'Dom Testa is the author of the Eric Swan thriller series, including the acclaimed debut, Power Trip. Get a free prequel short story at EricSwan.com.\\', \\'As of 2023, Dom has published more than two dozens books in multiple genres, both fiction and non-fiction, and under a variety of pen names.\\', \\'His Galahad series of science fiction novels is published under the name Tyber North. His other genres/names include middle grade fiction (as Buster Blank), fun facts/trivia (as Billy B. Good), and dark short fiction (as Harlan Plumber).\\', \\'Dom divides his time between Georgia and Colorado. See all of his titles at ProfoundGroup.com.\\']} Dom Testa (Author) Books Children\\'s Books Humor Review A book of imagination and wonder. -- Greg Moody, KCNC-TV Denver Galahad 1 should be on everyone\\'s bookshelf. -- Frances Owens, First Lady of Colorado Read it with your whole family and enjoy the ride. -- Michael Booth, Denver Post From the Inside Flap Trouble in deep space 251 teenagers, locked inside the ship known as Galahad, on their own, with no help from Earth\\x85from anyone. And now someone is threatening to destroy the ship and everyone on board. \"If we don\\x92t get to the bottom of this pretty soon there\\x92s going to be some real trouble on this ship.\" Triana sat forward. \"You\\x92re talking about the effects on the crew.\" \"Yes, I am,\" Gap said. \"When Peter freaked out, it was unsettling, but not surprising. But this...\" Lita Marques set down her stylus pen and spoke up. \"Gap\\x92s right. Someone is intentionally trying to scare us.\" Triana said, \"I wanted all of the crewmembers to relax and get used to their new lives. That\\x92s pretty hard to do when someone is threatening your life. It could be any one of us, even someone right here in this room.\" The statement was followed by dead silence. Each of the Council members exchanged glances. Gap exhaled loudly. \\x91There\\x92s only one problem,\\x92 he thought to himself. \\x91What if this person doesn\\x92t have a ticket to be on this flight?\\x92 The first volume in Dom Testa\\x92s breath-taking new adventure saga\\x85 GALAHAD 1 THE COMET\\x92S CURSE About the Author Dom Testa, a radio host since 1977, currently stars on the popular \"Dom and Jane Show\" on Mix 100 in Denver. A strong advocate of literacy programs, he regularly visits Colorado schools, reading to more than 500 kids each year. Dom began \"The Big Brain Club\" to encourage students to overcome the peer pressure that often prevents them from achieving their true potential. Excerpt. © Reprinted by permission. All rights reserved. There are few sights more beautiful. For all of the spectacular sunsets along a beach, or vivid rainbows arcing over a mist-covered forest, or high mountain pastures exploding with wildflowers, nothing could compare to this. This embraced every breath-taking scene. Mother Earth, in all of her supreme glory, spinning in a showcase of wonder. No picture, no television image, no movie scene could ever do her justice. From two hundred miles up it\\x92s spellbinding, hypnotic. Which made saying goodbye even more difficult. The ship sat still and silent in the cold, airless vacuum of space. It was a massive vessel, but against the backdrop of the planet below it appeared small, a child teetering at the feet of a parent, preparing to take its first steps. Soft, twinkling lights at the edges helped to define the shape which could not easily be described. Portions of it were boxy, others rectangular, with several curves and angles that seemed awkward. To an untrained eye it appeared as if it had simply been thrown together from leftover parts. In a way, that was true. Its dark, grayish-blue surface was speckled by hundreds of small windows. 251 pairs of eyes peered out, eyes mostly wet with tears, getting a final glimpse of home. 251 colonists sealed inside, and not one over the age of sixteen. Their thoughts and feelings contained a single thread: each envisioned family members two hundred miles below, grouped together outside, staring up into the sky. Some would be shielding their eyes from the glare of the sun, unable to see the ship but knowing that it was up there, somewhere. Others, on the dark side of the planet, would be sifting through the maze of stars, hoping to pick out the quiet flicker of light, pointing, embracing, crying. Many were too ill and unable to leave their bed, but were likely gazing out their own windows, not wanting to loosen the emotional grip on their son or daughter so far away. The day filled with both hope and dread had arrived. With a slight shudder, the ship came to life. It began to push away from the space station where it had been magnetically tethered for two years. Inside the giant steel shell there was no sensation of movement other than the image of the orbiting station gradually sliding past the windows. That was enough to impress upon the passengers that the voyage had begun. Galahad had launched. After a few moments Triana Martell turned away from one of the windows and, with a silent sigh, began to walk away. Unlike her fellow shipmates her eyes remained dry, unable, it seemed, to cry anymore. \"Hey, Tree,\" she heard a voice call out behind her. \"Don\\x92t you want to watch?\" \"You won\\x92t notice anything,\" she said over her shoulder. \"It might be hours before you can tell any difference in the size. We won\\x92t have enough speed for a while.\" \"Yeah,\" came another voice, \"but you won\\x92t ever see it again. Don\\x92t you want to say goodbye?\" Triana slipped around a corner of the well-lit hallway, and when she answered it was mostly to herself. \"I\\x92ve already said my goodbyes.\" With the entire crew\\x92s attention focused on the outside view, she had the corridor to herself, and appreciated it. Read more Deadly particles in a comet\\'s tail have altered the Earth\\'s atmosphere. The only hope for saving mankind is to select the brightest young people from around the world and launch them towards a new home, light-years away. But trouble has also boarded Galahad, and it could spell disaster. The ship\\'s Council, with help from the most incredible computer ever created, must battle fear, jealousy, and time...before it\\'s too late. Original.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0857621874', 'average_rating': 4.5}, page_content='HAND LETTERING /ANGLAIS Paperback – September 7, 2017 None None Books Arts & Photography Other Media  Everything you need to know to create your own bespoke lettering, this is the one book you need to get started in hand lettering! With more than 50 complete and inspirational alphabets in an amazing range of hand-lettered styles, including specially commissioned alphabets from 8 international hand letterers and designers, this is the complete guide to creating your own bespoke alphabet. \\xa0From sketching it out to inking it up, artist, illustrator and hand-letterer Thy Doan Graves provides advice on using a variety of materials from brush pens to Sharpies. There are even 16 \"your turn\" pages for you to practice your new lettering skills, so when it comes to writing those wedding invitations or place settings your hand drawn alphabet will turn out perfect!'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': 'B01FR3FEFU', 'average_rating': 3.4}, page_content='Sallowed Blood Kindle Edition {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amzn-author-media-prod/3596coag6mqv8knv8r8lnjhr69._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Stuart G. Yates\\', \\'about\\': [\"These are difficult times for so many of us, uncertainty and unease, constant companions. A good book can help us all to escape to a different world. As a writer, I\\'m fortunate that I can create new worlds or visit old ones. I hope you can join me as I sit here, at my home in Spain and do my best to do what I do best!\", \"Mine is not a rags to riches story or one borne out of hardship, the need to write to pay bills, or the result of a college course. I write because I love it and I always strive to make my work as enjoyable as possible. Writing in several genres allows me to weave all sorts of different stories, from Westerns to thrillers to historical fiction. Readers can slip into another world and come out feeling breathless, excited, desperate for more. Sometimes I succeed, sometimes I don\\'t, but I try my best.\", \"I\\'m blessed with a good imagination. I don\\'t know where my stories come from and I can structure a novel because I read and, as Stephen King once said about the way he learned, I love movies. I see the novel I write as a movie played out in my head. The better I can do this, the better my book. There is no magic formula, no matter what you might read, and there is no easy route to success. It\\'s just hard work and a determination not to give in. When I found my first publisher back in 2009 I thought my dreams had come true. My lifelong ambition to be a novelist. Well, I was wrong. My publisher was a crook and I got ripped off. I should have stuck it out for an agent, but I was impatient. I wrote my first novel at the age of sixteen, but despite many attempts, no one would publish me. The years were passing by far too quickly but when another publisher accepted my work 30 years after my first submission, I knew I was doing something right. But that elusive deal with one of the big boys, well, that\\'s still to arrive and I continue to try and acquire a literary agent that will help me on my journey.\", \"I\\'ve worked at a lot of jobs and now I\\'m a teacher. I love teaching, I truly do. The kids keep me young! Sometimes, they even buy my books. Or their parents do. Writing, however, will always be my passion.\", \"I write stories which will appeal to those of you who like cracking good tales, with lots of mystery, thrills, suspense. Above all else, I write what I enjoy. I have a broad taste. It\\'s reflected in what I create. But, whatever the genre, the main point is always the story!\", \\'Dip into my catalogue here on Amazon and try one for yourself.\\', \\'Thank you for dropping by and happy reading.\\']} Stuart G. Yates (Author)   Format: Kindle Edition Books Mystery, Thriller & Suspense Mystery  In the dark corners of a castle deep in the Alps, a secret awaits Daniel Stone. After inheriting the castle from his grandmother, Daniel and his father travel to Bavaria.They soon notice a dark presence in the old stronghold: strange noises echo from the depths beneath the castle, and someone or something seems to be following their every move.After things spiral out of control, Daniel and his father receive unexpected help from an old relative, who tells them of the dark secrets the castle holds. But even with the three of them, will they be able to discover the centuries-old mystery that lies buried, or will darkness claim them all?'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0140058451', 'average_rating': 4.7}, page_content='The Iron Wolf and Other Stories Mass Market Paperback – December 9, 1987 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71wGgb2tkDL._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Richard Adams\\', \\'about\\': [\\'Richard George Adams (born 9 May, 1920) is best-remembered as the author of Watership Down, but wrote many other novels, short stories, poems and a biography.\\', \"He originally began telling the story of Watership Down to his two daughters, Juliet and Rosamond, on a trip to Stratford-on-Avon, to see a play. They insisted he publish the tale as a book. When Watership Down was finally published, it sold over a million copies in record time in both the United Kingdom and the United States. Watership Down has become a modern classic and won both the Carnegie Medal and the Guardian Children\\'s Fiction Prize in 1972.\", \"Others of his books include Shardik, Maia, Tales from Watership Down, The Girl in a Swing and The Plague Dogs, the last two of which, together with Watership Down, have been filmed. His goal was always to tell a good story, ideally one so good you can\\'t put it down! His last work, \\'The Adventures of Eggbox Dragon\\', which is a picture-book for younger children, will be published posthumously by Hodder in 2017. It was written when he was 93.\", \"During his later years Richard and his wife Elizabeth lived in Whitchurch, Hampshire, very close to Watership Down, and not far from where they had both grown up. He wrote about his childhood and youth, including the time he served in the army in World War II, in his biography \\'The Day Gone By\\'.\", \\'During the last year of his life he kept a blog: https://www.watership-down.com/blog/. He died peacefully on Christmas Eve 2016.\\']} Richard Adams (Author) Books Literature & Fiction Short Stories & Anthologies  NEW HARD TO FIND SOFTCOVER COLLECTIBLE.'),\n",
