       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '1704656621', 'average_rating': 4.6}, page_content=\"Unicorn Activity Book for Kids Ages 4-8: Fun with UNICORN Adventure. Children’s Workbook Activity Game for Learning, Coloring, Mazes, Sudoku for Kids, Dot To Dot and More Paperback – Large Print, November 2, 2019 None Michelle G. Peltier (Author) Books Children's Books Activities, Crafts & Games  UNICORN GIFTS / THE BEST GIFT IDEA FOR GIRLS Unicorn Activity Book for Kids Ages 4-8 activity books for kids ages 4-8, activity books for kids, unicorn book, coloring activity book, kids activity booksWith beautiful coloring and more activity pages.Your Kids will enjoy with various activites.Incredibly Fun and RelaxingWhat's inside the book:- Coloring Cute Unicorn- Dot-to-Dot- Maze- Sudoku for kids- Find the correct Shadow- Unicorn Body Part and Easy word- Paste the number- Unicorn Easy Drawing- Learning Easy Time- Find the way to Unicorn- Mathematical Mazeunicorn activity book, coloring activity book, unicorn activity books, kids activity books ages 4-8, 5 year old activity books, activity books for kids ages 4-8, colored books for kids, unicorn activity books for kids ages 4-8, travel activity books for kids, kid book, unicorn coloring book, unicorn book, activity book, coloring activity book, kid activity book, kid coloring book, books girls age 6, girl coloring book, unicorn kid book, 4 year old girl books,\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'parent_asin': '0385478550', 'average_rating': 4.6}, page_content='The Magdalene Gospel Hardcover – September 1, 1995 {\\'avatar\\': \\'https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/A1RcP43zqTL._SY600_.jpg\\', \\'name\\': \\'Mary Ellen Ashcroft\\', \\'about\\': [\\'Mary Ellen Ashcroft grew up in Washington State and came to Minnesota via England and South Africa. An active wilderness guide and vicar of a start-up Episcopal Church, she loves paddling, biking, hiking, knitting, and playing with her grandchildren. After being an English professor for many years, Ashcroft moved to northern Minnesota, where she looks out at Lake Superior every morning.\\']} Mary Ellen Ashcroft (Author) Books Christian Books & Bibles From Publishers Weekly From the title and from the subtitle?\"What if women had written the Gospels?\"?one might expect this book to resemble other, politicized, feminist retellings of the biblical gospels. Nothing could be farther from the truth. Ashcroft\\'s Magdalene is a graceful theological reflection presented through a series of imaginative memoirs. Jesus has been crucified, and 10 of his female disciples gather on Holy Saturday to talk about his impact on their lives. In a male-dominated society, Jesus has given them?women at the margins, every one of them?hope and self-respect. If the retrospective theology seems advanced for a pre-Resurrection gathering, the stories themselves are simple, sweet and often moving. Ashcroft\\'s comments in the endnotes, however, are harder hitting: there her sources include both scripture and feminist scholarship. As a result, this is that rare book, the one that will appeal equally to traditionalists and progressives. Copyright 1995 Reed Business Information, Inc. From Library Journal Although Mary Magdalene and other women were faithful followers of Jesus, the stories of their discipleship have seldom been told. In the canonical Gospels, at least, the stories of the women\\'s discovery of Jesus\\' empty tomb are met with silence and disbelief. Ashcroft (English, Bethel Coll.) recovers the voices of these women in an imaginative retelling of their lives and faith. Hear the story of Lydia, suffering from a hemorrhage, and the ways that the touch of Jesus\\' garment healed her. Or listen to the story of Martha, Mary, Jesus, and the raising of Lazarus. From these voices emerge the power of story as a means of remembrance and the power of community to heal grief and sorrow. A nice addition for most libraries.Copyright 1995 Reed Business Information, Inc. From the Publisher Jesus touched the lives of many women with compassion, love, and forgiveness. However, the story of the women who followed Jesus goes almost unnoticed in the gospels. The Magdalene Gospel shatters the centuries of silence imposed on these women. Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of Jesus, and others devoted their lives to Jesus; they gave up everything for him, because he had given them everything. As Jesus gave his life for them, these women shared his pain at the foot of the cross, and risked their lives by caring for his crucified body. In the dark nights and gloomy days between Jesus\\' death and his resurrection, Mary Magdalene and the other women tried to make sense of their Lord\\'s tragic end. This is their story. The Magdalene Gospel tells the very personal, moving stories of how Jesus changed people\\'s lives. Stricken with the unspeakable pain of losing Jesus, Mary Magdalene and her friends grieve, cry, and care for one another. They emerge from this dark hour by caring for others, as Jesus had cared for them. Weakly, but then with increasing strength, they give voice to the depth of their love of Jesus and their reasons for following him. In sharing their stories, Mary Magdalene and her sister mourners begin to shed the burden of grief. No other book allows women disciples to tell their own stories. This fresh perspective, presented in a captivatingly personal, yet very accessible style, enlivens the well-known story of Jesus. The Magdalene Gospel is good news for everyone. From the Inside Flap Jesus touched the lives of many women with\\xa0\\xa0compassion, love, and forgiveness. However, the story of\\xa0\\xa0the women who followed Jesus goes almost unnoticed\\xa0\\xa0in the gospels. The Magdalene\\xa0\\xa0Gospel shatters the centuries of silence imposed on\\xa0\\xa0these women. Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of\\xa0\\xa0Jesus, and others devoted their lives to Jesus; they\\xa0\\xa0gave up everything for him, because he had given\\xa0\\xa0them everything. As Jesus gave his life for them,\\xa0\\xa0these women shared his pain at the foot of the\\xa0\\xa0cross, and risked their lives by caring for his\\xa0\\xa0crucified body. In the dark nights and gloomy days\\xa0\\xa0between Jesus\\' death and his resurrection, Mary\\xa0\\xa0Magdalene and the other women tried to make sense of\\xa0\\xa0their Lord\\'s tragic end. This is their story. The Magdalene Gospel tells the very\\xa0\\xa0personal, moving stories of how Jesus changed people\\'s\\xa0\\xa0lives. Stricken with the unspeakable pain of\\xa0\\xa0losing Jesus, Mary Magdalene and her friends grieve,\\xa0\\xa0cry, and care for one another. They emerge from this\\xa0\\xa0dark hour by caring for others, as Jesus had cared\\xa0\\xa0for them. Weakly, but then with increasing\\xa0\\xa0strength, they give voice to the depth of their love of\\xa0\\xa0Jesus and their reasons for following him. In\\xa0\\xa0sharing their stories, Mary Magdalene and her sister\\xa0\\xa0mourners begin to shed the burden of grief. No other\\xa0\\xa0book allows women disciples to tell their own\\xa0\\xa0stories. This fresh perspective, presented in a\\xa0\\xa0captivatingly personal, yet very accessible style,\\xa0\\xa0enlivens the well-known story of Jesus. The\\xa0\\xa0Magdalene Gospel is good news for\\xa0\\xa0everyone. Read more Jesus touched the lives of many women with\\xa0\\xa0compassion, love, and forgiveness. However, the 